The correction. A/p is perfect, and it is d-adically complete, because a perfect ring has bounded d-power torsion. Hence (A/I)^♭ = lim_{x↦x^p} A/(p, d) ≅ A/p. So A_inf(A/I) ≅ W(A/p) ≅ A by Corollary 2.31, with θ corresponding to A → A/I. Hence ker θ = I = (d) is principal, which also gives FG ≃ id directly. Add one sentence to the note of item 19 saying that the proof must establish (A/I)^♭ ≅ A/p, or ker θ principal, before invoking [BMS1, Remark 3.11].

